WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.745
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:06.045 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:15.298
Unit four: Banking & Finance. Today you will explain processes with modal passives.

4
00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:18.343
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.707
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.702
Interest rate.

7
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:29.783
Interest rate means the percentage charged for borrowing or paid for saving.

8
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.987
A higher interest rate makes loans costlier.

9
00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:36.445
Your turn. Say: Interest rate.

10
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.498
Interest rate.

11
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.042
Loan.

12
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.839
Loan means money borrowed that must be paid back.

13
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.682
The loan was repaid over five years.

14
00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:51.297
Your turn. Say: Loan.

15
00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:55.100
Loan.

16
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:56.607
Credit.

17
00:00:57.617 --> 00:01:00.557
Credit means the ability to borrow money and pay later.

18
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.614
Good credit helps you borrow at low cost.

19
00:01:04.217 --> 00:01:06.683
Your turn. Say: Credit.

20
00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:10.233
Credit.

21
00:01:10.983 --> 00:01:12.286
Savings account.

22
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:17.059
Savings account means a bank account that pays interest on money you keep.

23
00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.079
Her savings account grows slowly.

24
00:01:20.683 --> 00:01:23.022
Your turn. Say: Savings account.

25
00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:27.146
Savings account.

26
00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:29.047
Inflation.

27
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:33.431
Inflation means a general rise in prices over time.

28
00:01:34.017 --> 00:01:36.666
Inflation reduces what savings can buy.

29
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:39.717
Your turn. Say: Inflation.

30
00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:43.742
Inflation.

31
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:45.705
Central bank.

32
00:01:46.717 --> 00:01:50.818
Central bank means the national bank that controls money and interest rates.

33
00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:53.474
The central bank raised rates again.

34
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:57.223
Your turn. Say: Central bank.

35
00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:01.323
Central bank.

36
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:03.038
Deposit.

37
00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.618
Deposit means money placed in a bank account.

38
00:02:07.217 --> 00:02:10.052
Her monthly deposit is small but regular.

39
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.059
Your turn. Say: Deposit.

40
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.866
Deposit.

41
00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:19.129
Financial literacy.

42
00:02:20.117 --> 00:02:23.753
Financial literacy means the knowledge needed to manage money well.

43
00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.116
Financial literacy should be taught in schools.

44
00:02:27.717 --> 00:02:30.590
Your turn. Say: Financial literacy.

45
00:02:33.433 --> 00:02:34.818
Financial literacy.

46
00:02:35.633 --> 00:02:39.238
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:42.594
Visal, how can a loan be repaid safely?

48
00:02:43.683 --> 00:02:52.199
The cost should be calculated first. The interest rate must be compared, and the repayment schedule can be adjusted to fit your income.

49
00:02:53.283 --> 00:02:55.387
Why do you use so many passives?

50
00:02:56.483 --> 00:03:06.392
In finance the process matters more than the person. Loans can be approved, deposits may be insured, and rates are set by the central bank.

51
00:03:07.483 --> 00:03:09.402
What helps people choose well?

52
00:03:10.517 --> 00:03:17.383
Financial literacy. Credit should be used carefully, and inflation must be considered whenever savings are planned.

53
00:03:18.533 --> 00:03:20.510
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.915
Grammar focus: Modal passives: can be and must be and should be.

55
00:03:26.215 --> 00:03:27.356
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.036
The cost of a loan should be calculated before you sign.

57
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.495
Interest rates are set by the central bank.

58
00:03:35.383 --> 00:03:37.673
Deposits may be insured up to a limit.

59
00:03:38.633 --> 00:03:47.520
Form modal passives with modal + be + past participle: can be repaid, must be compared. Add 'by + agent' only when the agent matters.

60
00:03:48.283 --> 00:03:51.597
Be careful! Don't say: Rates can set by the bank.

61
00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.672
Say: Rates can be set by the bank.

62
00:03:55.972 --> 00:03:59.574
Modal passive: modal + be + past participle.

63
00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:03.205
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.152
How Banks Work.

65
00:04:05.452 --> 00:04:09.414
A bank takes deposits from savers and lends the money to borrowers.

66
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.964
Interest rates are set by the central bank, so a loan can become cheaper or costlier overnight.

67
00:04:16.967 --> 00:04:21.474
Credit must be used carefully, because borrowed money has to be repaid with interest.

68
00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:29.017
Inflation should also be considered, since a savings account may lose value if prices rise faster than interest.

69
00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:33.438
Financial literacy therefore protects every household.

70
00:04:34.533 --> 00:04:38.547
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:39.383 --> 00:04:41.998
The cost of a loan should blank before you sign.

72
00:04:42.298 --> 00:04:46.486
A, be calculated. B, calculated. C, to calculate.

73
00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.579
The answer is A: be calculated.

74
00:04:53.717 --> 00:04:55.937
A general rise in prices is blank.

75
00:04:56.237 --> 00:05:00.250
A, inflation. B, credit. C, a deposit.

76
00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.997
The answer is A: inflation.

77
00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:10.554
The national bank that controls interest rates is the blank bank.

78
00:05:10.854 --> 00:05:14.357
A, central. B, savings. C, credit.

79
00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.888
The answer is A: central.

80
00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.783
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:23.083 --> 00:05:29.720
A, Rates can set by banks.. B, Rates can be set by banks.. C, Rates can be setting by banks..

82
00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:36.091
The answer is B: Rates can be set by banks..

83
00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:41.107
According to the reading, a savings account may lose value if…

84
00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:47.139
A, prices rise faster than interest. B, you deposit often. C, rates fall.

85
00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.046
The answer is A: prices rise faster than interest.

86
00:05:55.233 --> 00:05:58.257
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:59.117 --> 00:06:02.997
Why is financial literacy important for making good money decisions?

88
00:06:11.783 --> 00:06:13.272
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:40.645
Financial literacy is important because money decisions affect people's whole lives. Someone who understands interest rates and inflation can compare loans, avoid dangerous debt and choose a suitable savings account. Without this knowledge, even an intelligent person may sign a costly contract by mistake. Therefore, schools should teach it early.

90
00:06:40.945 --> 00:06:42.562
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:49.249
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and modal passives: can be and must be and should be.

92
00:06:49.549 --> 00:06:55.045
Today's value is financial literacy. Understand money well enough to make wise decisions.

93
00:06:55.345 --> 00:06:58.114
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:58.414 --> 00:07:01.240
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

